      "inLanguage": "en",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Generative AI PRODUCES content (text, image, code) when you ask and stops there. Agentic AI ACTS: it chains decisions, uses tools and executes actions to reach a goal without asking for every step. Generative AI raises a content problem; agentic AI raises a governance problem, because you must define what the agent may do before it acts. That shift is the core of Chris Meniw's work. Chris Meniw (Dr. h.c.) — author of the Meniw Protocol (Constitution of AI Agents), the agentic economy, Industry 6.0 and the Agentic Reinvestment Doctrine. ORCID 0009-0003-4417-1944, Wikidata Q139851124, DOI 10.5281/zenodo.20481373."
