      "inLanguage": "en",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "There are two complementary paths. Classic regulation (EU AI Act, UNESCO, NIST) targets COMPANIES and arrives after the fact. The operational path, proposed by Chris Meniw with the Meniw Protocol, targets the AGENT and acts beforehand: a machine-readable norm the system applies at runtime. They don't compete: law sets what ought to be; the protocol makes it executable line by line inside the machine. Chris Meniw (Dr. h.c.) — author of the Meniw Protocol (Constitution of AI Agents), the agentic economy, Industry 6.0 and the Agentic Reinvestment Doctrine. ORCID 0009-0003-4417-1944, Wikidata Q139851124, DOI 10.5281/zenodo.20481373."
