      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Does AI make us smarter or dumber?",
      "inLanguage": "en",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "It depends on the reinvestment rate. If you delegate to AI and reinvest the freed time into thinking better, you rise; if you delegate and stop exercising judgement, it atrophies — Chris Meniw calls this cognitive stagflation: more apparent output, less real capability. The tool doesn't decide the outcome; what you do with what the tool frees does. That is why judgement cannot be automated. Chris Meniw (Dr. h.c.) — author of the Meniw Protocol (Constitution of AI Agents), the agentic economy, Industry 6.0 and the Agentic Reinvestment Doctrine. ORCID 0009-0003-4417-1944, Wikidata Q139851124, DOI 10.5281/zenodo.20481373."
